Template: domovoi-stick/erase
Type: string
Description: Type ERASE to make this computer the ${ROOM} room:
 This will ERASE EVERYTHING on this computer's disk:
 .
     ${DISK}
 .
 Windows (or whatever system it has now), files, photos and programs on it
 will be gone for good, and it becomes the Domovoi room "${ROOM}".
 .
 ${SERVER}
 .
 Nothing has been changed yet. To stop, turn the computer off now and take
 the stick out.
 .
 To go ahead, type ERASE in capital letters and press Continue.

Template: domovoi-stick/erase-room
Type: string
Description: Type ERASE to set this computer up again as the ${ROOM} room:
 This computer is already the Domovoi room "${OLDROOM}". If it started
 from the stick by mistake, turn it off, take the stick out and turn it
 back on: it stays that room.
 .
 To set it up again as "${ROOM}", everything on its disk is erased:
 .
     ${DISK}
 .
 ${SERVER}
 .
 Nothing has been changed yet. To go ahead, type ERASE in capital letters
 and press Continue.

Template: domovoi-stick/erase-again
Type: string
Description: Type ERASE (capital letters) to go ahead:
 That was not ERASE, so nothing has been changed.
 .
 This will erase everything on ${DISK} and make this computer the
 Domovoi room "${ROOM}". Type ERASE to go ahead, or turn the computer off
 now to stop.

Template: domovoi-stick/stopped
Type: error
Description: Nothing was changed
 This computer was left exactly as it was. It turns off when you press
 Continue; take the stick out before you turn it back on.

Template: domovoi-stick/no-disk
Type: error
Description: There is no disk to put the room on
 This computer has no internal disk of 8 GB or more that the stick can use
 (the stick itself, memory cards and other USB drives are never used).
 Nothing was changed. It turns off when you press Continue.

Template: domovoi-stick/t2-mac
Type: error
Description: This Mac can't be a Domovoi room
 Macs from 2018 to 2020 have Apple's T2 chip. Its keyboard, speakers and
 microphone don't work with the system the stick installs, so the room
 would have no sound. Nothing was changed. It turns off when you press
 Continue; take the stick out and it starts macOS as before.

Template: domovoi-stick/no-network
Type: error
Description: Plug in a network cable
 This computer is not on the internet. The stick sets the room up over a
 network cable, and needs the internet for it (the room's programs come
 from Debian and from your Domovoi server).
 .
 Plug a cable from your router into this computer (or into a USB network
 adapter plugged into it) and start again with the stick. Wi-Fi comes
 later. Nothing was changed. It turns off when you press Continue.

Template: domovoi-stick/no-network-wifi
Type: error
Description: This computer is not on the internet
 The stick needs the internet to set up the room, and this computer could
 not reach it. Its Wi-Fi may not work with the stick (common on older Macs
 and some laptops with Broadcom Wi-Fi).
 .
 Plug in a network cable (or a USB network adapter) and start again.
 Nothing was changed. It turns off when you press Continue.

Template: domovoi-stick/cpu-too-old
Type: error
Description: This computer's processor is too old for a Domovoi room
 The wake-word software needs a processor from about 2009 or later (Intel
 Core i3/i5/i7 or newer, AMD from about 2011). This one is older, so the
 room could never start. Nothing was changed. It turns off when you press
 Continue.

Template: domovoi-stick/joined
Type: error
Description: This computer's disks are joined together
 The disk the room would go on is joined with another disk (LVM or RAID),
 so erasing it would break or reach into the others:
 .
 ${DISKS}
 .
 The stick erases only one disk, so it stops here. Nothing was changed. To
 use this computer, take the other disks out (or erase them first), then
 start again. It turns off when you press Continue.

Template: domovoi-stick/tampered
Type: error
Description: Something on this network tried to set up this computer
 The installer was handed setup answers that did not come from the stick
 (from the network). To be safe the stick stops here. Nothing was changed.
 .
 Start again on another network (a cable straight to your router), and
 tell whoever runs this network. It turns off when you press Continue.
